From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] mfd, power: supply: mt6375: allow the 3 A of stock

Stock takes 3 A at the input and into the battery with a 3 A Type-C
current or a 5 V PD contract (mtk_pd_input_current_protection,
sc-charger-current, measured 3000 mA on stock). Move the limits there.
What goes above them is still refused.

On the device 5 V 3 A gave 2.74 A at 4.54 V and +1.25 A into the battery
with the screen on, where 2 A gave +0.4 A.

---
 drivers/mfd/mt6375.c                  | 16 ++++++++--------
 drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c | 17 +++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/mt6375.c b/drivers/mfd/mt6375.c
index aef5c7c..20c04ae 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/mt6375.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/mt6375.c
@@ -72,16 +72,16 @@ enum {
  * device tree asks for. These are values of the stock tree of the Lenovo
  * TB375FC for charging through this chip: 4.34 V (maintenance-v20-level0-cv and
  * maintenance-v10-level3-cv, the lowest of its battery maintenance table, which
- * a battery of any age can take), an input of 2 A (ac-charger-input-current)
- * and a charge current of 2 A (ichg). Stock goes to 4.5 V (battery-cv) with
- * battery maintenance off, and to 3 A with a 3 A Type-C current, which stay
- * out. AICR holds 100 mA from selector 2 up in steps of 25 mA, CV 3.9 V from 0
- * in steps of 10 mV, and ICHG 300 mA from 6 in steps of 50 mA, as in the
- * MediaTek driver.
+ * a battery of any age can take), and an input and a charge current of 3 A
+ * (sc-charger-current, and what stock takes from a 3 A Type-C current or a 5 V
+ * PD contract). Stock goes to 4.5 V (battery-cv) with battery maintenance off,
+ * which stays out. AICR holds 100 mA from selector 2 up in steps of 25 mA, CV
+ * 3.9 V from 0 in steps of 10 mV, and ICHG 300 mA from 6 in steps of 50 mA, as
+ * in the MediaTek driver.
  */
-#define MT6375_AICR_SEL_MAX	78
+#define MT6375_AICR_SEL_MAX	118
 #define MT6375_CV_SEL_MAX	44
-#define MT6375_ICHG_SEL_MAX	40
+#define MT6375_ICHG_SEL_MAX	60
 
 /*
  * A bad read before a read-modify-write can bring any value here, and setting
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c
index 0d2c6f4..8a8625e 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6375-charger.c
@@ -93,16 +93,17 @@
  * The most this driver ever asks for, from the stock tree: 4.34 V
  * (maintenance-v20-level0-cv, maintenance-v10-level3-cv), the lowest of its
  * battery maintenance table, which a battery of any age can take, a charge
- * current of 2 A (ichg, ac-charger-current) and an input of 2 A
- * (ac-charger-input-current). Stock also goes to 4.5 V (battery-cv) with
- * battery maintenance off, and to 3 A with a 3 A Type-C current, which stay out
- * here. A battery description above these is refused, and so is a value above
- * them from user space. The core driver has its own check of the same limits
- * for every write.
+ * current of 3 A (sc-charger-current) and an input of 3 A: what stock takes
+ * from a 3 A Type-C current or a 5 V PD contract, in mtk_basic_charger.c and
+ * mtk_pd_input_current_protection. Stock also goes to 4.5 V (battery-cv) with
+ * battery maintenance off, which stays out here. A 9 V contract is limited by
+ * its sink PDO, to the 2 A of that same function. A battery description above
